### NeXora — Admin end-to-end flow (REST Client / VS Code)
### Prerequisites: PostgreSQL, Redis, backend running on :8080

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@adminEmail = admin@nexora.com
@adminPassword = nexora123

### 1) Login as bootstrapped admin
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}",
  "deviceId": "rest-client"
}

###
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2) Profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 3) List departments (pick one name for category when creating users)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/departments
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4) List responder types (required for RESPONDER role)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/responder-types
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 5) Create NGO user (category = exact department name from step 3)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/ngo
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ngo_demo",
  "name": "Demo NGO",
  "contactNumber": "03001234567",
  "email": "ngo.demo@example.com",
  "password": "DemoPass123!",
  "category": "Search & Rescue Coordination"
}

### 6) Create responder (category = GOV department name + responderTypeId)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/responder
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "resp_demo",
  "name": "Demo Responder",
  "contactNumber": "03007654321",
  "email": "responder.demo@example.com",
  "password": "DemoPass123!",
  "category": "PDMA Operations",
  "responderTypeId": "P1"
}

### 7) Verify OTP for new portal user (check email / logs if mail disabled)
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-otp
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# {
#   "source": "ADMIN_USER",
#   "sourceId": "ngo_demo",
#   "purpose": "EMAIL_VERIFICATION",
#   "otp": "123456"
# }
